 {"sort_order": 5, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "name": "potato", "prep_note": "peeled, 1/2-inch cubes", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 6, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "name": "zucchini", "prep_note": "1/2-inch cubes", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 7, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "name": "granulated sugar", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 8, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "name": "soy sauce", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 9, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "name": "water", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 10, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "name": "cornstarch", "prep_note": "stirred into 3 tbsp water", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 11, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "lb", "name": "chinese wheat noodles", "prep_note": "thick fresh noodles, or udon", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 12, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "name": "cucumber", "prep_note": "cut in matchsticks, for serving", "is_optional": false}], "steps": ["Heat 2 tbsp oil in a skillet over medium heat. Fry the black bean paste 4-5 min, stirring, until it smells nutty and loosens. Scrape it into a bowl.", "Add the remaining oil and the pork. Cook 5 min, until browned. Add the onion and potato and cook 5 min.", "Stir in the zucchini, fried paste, sugar, soy sauce and water. Simmer 10 min, until the potato is tender.", "Stir the starch slurry and pour it in. Cook 1-2 min, until the sauce turns glossy and thick.", "Cook the noodles in boiling water per package directions, then drain and rinse.", "Divide the noodles among four bowls, spoon the sauce on top, and add cucumber."]}, {"slug": "kimbap", "title": "Kimbap (Seaweed Rice Rolls)", "cuisine": "Korean", "prep_time_min": 45, "cook_time_min": 15, "servings": 4, "spice_level": 0, "cookware": ["Skillet"], "notes": "Season the rice while it is warm; cold rice will not roll tightly.", "ingredients": [{"sort_order": 1, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "cup", "name": "short-grain rice", "prep_note": "cooked, warm", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 2, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "name": "toasted sesame oil", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 3, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "name": "salt", "prep_note": "divided", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 4, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "name": "egg", "prep_note": "beaten with a pinch of salt", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 5, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "name": "carrot", "prep_note": "cut in matchsticks", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 6, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "name": "spinach", "prep_note": "blanched, squeezed, tossed with 1/2 tsp sesame oil", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 7, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "oz", "name": "takuan", "prep_note": "cut in long strips", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 8, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "name": "cucumber", "prep_note": "seeded, cut in long strips", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 9, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "name": "fish cakes", "prep_note": "sliced in strips, pan-fried", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 10, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": "g", "name": "nori", "prep_note": "4 whole sheets, about 2.5 g each", "is_optional": false}, {"sort_order": 11, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "name": "vegetable oil", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false}], "steps": ["Mix the warm rice with sesame oil and half the salt. Spread it out to cool to room temperature.", "Heat a little vegetable oil in a skillet. Cook the beaten egg as a thin flat omelet, then slice into long strips.", "Saute the carrot in the same pan 2 min with the remaining salt, until barely tender.", "Lay a nori sheet shiny side down on a bamboo mat. Spread 3/4 cup rice over it, leaving 1 inch bare at the far edge.", "Lay a strip each of egg, carrot, spinach, takuan, cucumber and fish cake across the rice near you.", "Roll tightly, pressing as you go, and seal with a few grains of rice. Brush the roll